<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  DEALFLOW Refresh - the nightly chain (refresh-dealflow.bat), daily at 05:30.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (2026-09-21)
  Until today the ONLY definition of the job that rebuilds and publishes the board lived in
  desktop-setup/tasks/, which is gitignored - a Windows export embeds the exporting machine's
  principal SID and user paths, so it travels in the transfer bundle and never in git. The
  consequence is the one this audit ran into: the settings that decide whether the nightly fires
  at all - batteries, sleep, idle, the time limit - could not be read, diffed or reviewed from
  anywhere except the laptop itself, and MACHINE-HANDOFF.md section 4 is a prose summary rather
  than the thing that runs. The table that documents nine tasks had a tracked definition for one.

  THIS DOES NOT OVERRIDE THE LAPTOP. install-tasks.ps1 applies an export in tasks/ over a template
  of the same task name, always. So adding this changes nothing on a machine that already has the
  export; it gives every other machine the hardened definition instead of no definition, and it
  makes the settings below reviewable in a diff. Same contract as DealFlow_Cadence.xml.

  Placeholders, substituted by install-tasks.ps1: __REPO__ __PROFILE__ __USER__

  EVERY SETTING BELOW IS A PAID-FOR LESSON:

  * ExecutionTimeLimit PT6H. setup-automation.ps1 - still in the repo root - registers this same
    task with New-TimeSpan -Minutes 120, and install-tasks.ps1's own header records that PT2H
    "silently killed rebuild/publish for days". The measured full chain on 2026-09-20 ran 3h08m
    start to [5/5] commit. PT2H is under the real runtime; PT6H is slack.

  * StopOnIdleEnd FALSE, RestartOnIdle FALSE, RunOnlyIfIdle FALSE. The 2026-08-31 root cause,
    written up at the :end label of refresh-dealflow.bat: StopOnIdleEnd=true terminates the task
    the moment the machine stops being idle - i.e. the moment Alejandro sits down at it - which
    produced exit 255 at an hour that tracked when he woke up rather than any elapsed duration.
    Every PowerShell script in this repo that calls New-ScheduledTaskSettingsSet without an
    -IdleSettings object re-creates that default. This file states it instead of inheriting it.

  * DisallowStartIfOnBatteries FALSE, StopIfGoingOnBatteries FALSE. MACHINE-HANDOFF.md section 4
    records these as true on 6 of the 8 exported tasks. On the desktop that is inert. On the
    LAPTOP - which is the armed machine - true means the 05:30 run is skipped outright whenever
    the lid was on battery at 05:30, and killed mid-run if it is unplugged. A three-hour job on a
    laptop cannot carry either.

  * StartWhenAvailable TRUE with WakeToRun TRUE. Wake the box for the trigger, and catch up if the
    wake did not happen. Nothing in this chain mails a homeowner, so a late catch-up run is simply
    a late board - unlike DealFlow Cadence, which needs cadence-daily.bat's 08:00-20:00 window to
    make the same setting safe.

  * RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable FALSE, and this is the one place this template deliberately differs
    from DealFlow_Cadence.xml. Task Scheduler's network condition is evaluated by NLA, which after
    a 05:30 wake routinely reports no network for the seconds before the adapter associates - and
    a task declined for a condition writes NOTHING to leads-run.log. That is indistinguishable
    from a task that never fired, and distinguishing those two is exactly what costs a morning.
    refresh-dealflow.bat already opens with net_ready.py, which waits ~4 minutes and then REFUSES
    with a per-host reason in the log and rc=3. Prefer the refusal that explains itself over the
    silence that does not. Do not set this true without deleting that [0/5] block, and do not
    delete that block while this is false.

  * RestartOnFailure 2 x PT20M. New in this template. rc is now a real verdict - 1 scrape,
    2 compliance, 3 network, 4 health DOWN, 5 mirror, 6 gate refused - so a failure exit is
    finally something the scheduler can act on, and the single commonest one is rc=3, a network
    that was not up during one four-minute window. Retrying that at 05:50 and again at 06:10
    turns a lost day into a late board. MultipleInstancesPolicy IgnoreNew below is what makes it
    safe: a retry can never overlap a run that is still going.

  * MultipleInstancesPolicy IgnoreNew. Two refreshes at once would both scrape, both build, and
    both push.
-->
<Task version="1.2" xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/windows/2004/02/mit/task">
  <RegistrationInfo>
    <Author>__USER__</Author>
    <URI>\DEALFLOW Refresh</URI>
    <Description>DEALFLOW: nightly chain - scrape Miami-Dade/Broward/Palm Beach auctions, enrich, skip-trace phones, rebuild the board, run healthcheck + publish_guard, publish to the live site. Only the armed machine may run this - see MACHINE-HANDOFF.md section 1. Log: leads-run.log in the repo.</Description>
  </RegistrationInfo>
  <Triggers>
    <CalendarTrigger>
      <StartBoundary>2026-09-21T05:30:00</StartBoundary>
      <Enabled>true</Enabled>
      <ScheduleByDay>
        <DaysInterval>1</DaysInterval>
      </ScheduleByDay>
    </CalendarTrigger>
  </Triggers>
  <Principals>
    <Principal id="Author">
      <UserId>__USER__</UserId>
      <LogonType>InteractiveToken</LogonType>
      <RunLevel>LeastPrivilege</RunLevel>
    </Principal>
  </Principals>
  <Settings>
    <MultipleInstancesPolicy>IgnoreNew</MultipleInstancesPolicy>
    <DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>false</DisallowStartIfOnBatteries>
    <StopIfGoingOnBatteries>false</StopIfGoingOnBatteries>
    <AllowHardTerminate>true</AllowHardTerminate>
    <StartWhenAvailable>true</StartWhenAvailable>
    <RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>false</RunOnlyIfNetworkAvailable>
    <IdleSettings>
      <StopOnIdleEnd>false</StopOnIdleEnd>
      <RestartOnIdle>false</RestartOnIdle>
    </IdleSettings>
    <RestartOnFailure>
      <Interval>PT20M</Interval>
      <Count>2</Count>
    </RestartOnFailure>
    <AllowStartOnDemand>true</AllowStartOnDemand>
    <Enabled>true</Enabled>
    <Hidden>false</Hidden>
    <RunOnlyIfIdle>false</RunOnlyIfIdle>
    <WakeToRun>true</WakeToRun>
    <ExecutionTimeLimit>PT6H</ExecutionTimeLimit>
    <Priority>7</Priority>
  </Settings>
  <Actions Context="Author">
    <Exec>
      <Command>__REPO__\refresh-dealflow.bat</Command>
      <WorkingDirectory>__REPO__</WorkingDirectory>
    </Exec>
  </Actions>
</Task>
